{
  "chapter": "observability/cost-accounting",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Attribution is constructed at the gateway, not extracted from an invoice that has no",
    "tenant, no feature, and no run on it.",
    "Every call carries the price-table version it was priced under, so history does not",
    "silently reprice when a vendor changes a rate. Prices are integer micros per token,",
    "so the arithmetic is exact.",
    "Cached input is a separate meter, priced far below normal input. Folding the two into",
    "one field destroys the only signal that prefix discipline is working.",
    "Retries and abandoned branches cost full price, and eval traffic is its own bucket.",
    "The three add up to the total, so nothing hides.",
    "The distribution is over runs rather than calls, and it is percentiles rather than a",
    "mean, because run cost is heavy-tailed and the mean describes neither shape.",
    "topRunsShareBps covers the most expensive ceil(runs/100) runs — at these sample sizes",
    "that is one run, which is exactly the run worth finding."
  ],
  "prices": {
    "2026-01": {
      "atlas-1": { "input": 400, "cachedInput": 40, "output": 2000 },
      "atlas-mini": { "input": 80, "cachedInput": 8, "output": 320 }
    },
    "2026-06": {
      "atlas-1": { "input": 300, "cachedInput": 30, "output": 1500 },
      "atlas-mini": { "input": 60, "cachedInput": 6, "output": 240 }
    }
  },
